# the world over simulated days (Day length 30 min): the offices go round, the day turns, the abbot intones, cantors
# lead the antiphons, the verses go side to side, between two cantors or from a soloist to the choir; the low voices
# hold the ison or sing the organum; all in the chronicle. Nobody sings a wrong note, out of tune or against another
tap GLO
spin K1 -2
tap HOME
expect office 1
expect day 1
expect choir 6
wait 1800000
expect day 2
expect events >8
expect chron >0
expect cantor0 >7
expect sung2 >0
expect sung5 >0
expect notes >500
expect offmode 0
expect offtune 0
expect clash 0
expect gone 0
expect chrongone 0
shot day2.png
# Sext: a small choir (three), the ison
office 4
expect office 4
expect choir 3
wait 20000
shot sext.png
# the days: the novice is given the verses, then a solo, and in time takes his vows; a new novice comes to the gate
# (days N: N of the world's daily turns at once)
expect vowed1 0
expect part1 <30
days 30
expect vowed1 1
expect part1 >84
expect here6 1
tap ARP
wait 300
shot brothers30.png
tap HOME
days 60
expect here 7
wait 600000
shot later.png
expect day >90
expect offmode 0
expect offtune 0
expect clash 0
expect gone 0
expect chrongone 0
